# 9. Animation and Interaction

Use the existing Framer Motion and Three.js infrastructure wherever appropriate.

Create a coherent motion language:

- Gentle fade and translate transitions.
- Subtle reveal animations for section content.
- Controlled hover elevation on cards.
- Short transitions for buttons and navigation.
- Carefully timed hero animation.
- Subtle gradient movement only in selected areas.
- Smooth modal and mobile-menu transitions.

Avoid:

- Excessive scroll hijacking.
- Unnecessary page-wide motion.
- Constantly flashing gradients.
- Large movement on every card.
- Animations that delay access to content.
- Animations that interfere with reading or keyboard interaction.

Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Provide accessible alternatives for animated artwork and ensure essential content never depends on animation to appear.

Use lazy loading or deferred initialization for expensive 3D content when appropriate. Keep mobile performance in mind.

